# pocket — environment variables
#
# Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in. Agents working in this repo
# follow the rule in AGENTS.md: if a feature needs an API key, they will
# ask you to paste it in chat, walk you through where to get it, then
# append it here under its canonical name.
#
# Never commit .env. Never paste real secrets into .env.example.

# --- Pocket runtime --------------------------------------------------

# Override the repo root. Useful if you run `bin/pocket` from outside
# the repo and `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` won't find it.
# POCKET_ROOT=

# --- Model providers (add as needed) ---------------------------------

# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# --- Slack -----------------------------------------------------------

# Bot token (xoxb-...) from your Slack app's OAuth & Permissions page
# (https://api.slack.com/apps). Needs the chat:write scope.
# SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=

# Optional default destination for `pocket slack` when --to is omitted
# (channel ID, channel name like #general, or user ID like U0123…).
# SLACK_DEFAULT_CHANNEL=

# Optional destination for `pocket briefing` when --to is omitted
# (channel ID or user ID like U0123…). Defaults to Pietro's self-DM.
# SLACK_BRIEFING_TARGET=

# --- Gmail (for `pocket email`) --------------------------------------

# The Gmail address you send from.
# GMAIL_USER=

# A Google App Password (16 chars, not your account password). Generate
# one at https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords (requires 2FA).
# GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=

# --- Notion (for `pocket notion` / `pocket briefing` tickets) --------

# Internal integration token (secret_...) from
# https://www.notion.so/my-integrations. Share the tickets database with
# the integration so it can read it.
# NOTION_TOKEN=

# The "M&S Tickets" database id (the 32-char id in the database URL).
# NOTION_TICKETS_DB=

# Your Notion person id — scopes the default `notion tickets` view and the
# briefing to tickets assigned to you. Omit to always see everyone's.
# NOTION_USER_ID=
